Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:35:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: sound: Add Apple S8000 MCA
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The A9 MCA ("mca-version 4") is an I2S serializer fed by SmartIO DMA.
Each MCA has a 32-bit MCLK control word next to the shared i2s-switch,
which the driver exports as a clock for the codec's MCLK, and a route in
the i2s-switch between its switch node (audN) and the pad its codec is
wired to (pinN).

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 09b32848, e9fce91b and 3e47c1c2 (J71t
 ledger 10.5); the MCLK word, MCLK rate and SmartIO shim words moved to
 the driver's match data, the raw i2s-switch register/value pairs became
 the switch node and pad index in the apple,i2s-switch phandle
 arguments, and the PIO properties went with the timer PCM. DMA and the
 power domain are required.]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
